    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Glendale’s official symbol is a black squirrel, a nod to the town’s playful wildlife heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glendale%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village runs its own wastewater treatment plant and artesian well water plant, keeping local water self‑sufficient.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glendale%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Twenty‑five squirrel statues in quirky outfits adorn Glendale’s streets, echoing Cincinnati’s Big Pig Gig tradition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
